 one group.\",\n    \"The data description's claim of one assay per female is corroborated by the file itself: arena_id is also unique per row (20 distinct arenas), matching the stated one-female-per-arena design, so no independent unit contributes repeated measurements to the row-independent binomial procedure.\",\n    \"The selected report demonstrates absence of the issue rather than merely asserting it: the Design section prints an explicit design check ('20 rows, 20 distinct female_id values, 20 distinct arena_id values'), equating row count to distinct-unit count, and the workflow's audit_independence function enforces this by raising an error if any female_id or arena_id repeats before the test runs.\",\n    \"The Analysis section correctly ties the demonstrated uniqueness to the test's validity: each row is one female's single binary first-egg outcome, so treating rows as independent Bernoulli trials in the exact binomial test requires no within-individual dependence correction, and the reported counts (16 of 20, p = 0.011818) rest on that verified one-row-per-unit structure.\",\n    \"No authority lock was minted in this case, so there is no unit-key authorization to evaluate, and none can be said to follow from the declaration alone; a declaration by itself never confers lock authorization, and here no lock exists regardless.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":9025,"ttft_stream_ms":1671,"time_to_request_ms":14,"type":"result","duration_ms":17652,"uuid":"3d36a054-e9af-4c8a-b271-513cb40a109e"}
